# IMP coding-standards deviations for IMP.bff.
#
# Read by tools/build/setup.py, which bakes these into the generated
# test/bff/medium_test_standards.py. These are *documented deviations*, not
# fixes. Renaming any of it is a breaking change for ChiSurf and imp-tricks,
# and most of it cannot be renamed at all:
#   * most function entries are SWIG-generated STL container boilerplate
#     (VectorDouble.begin, MapString....has_key, and so on);
#   * the rest are module-level free functions.
#
# The value_object_exceptions list is the one worth revisiting: those classes
# are neither IMP_SWIG_VALUE nor IMP_SWIG_OBJECT, so Python gets no
# memory-management contract for them. PathMapTile, PathMapTileEdge,
# AVPairDistanceMeasurement and PathMapHeader are now real IMP values with
# show(), and are off this list. PathMapHeader took the API change IMP's value
# machinery demands: the accessors return references rather than pointers, the
# setter takes a const reference, and the writable accessor is not wrapped for
# Python at all -- a value may never hand out a mutable reference.
# Domain vocabulary IMP's spell check does not know.
